3. Why
   The source PDF is encrypted with an empty user password and permission bits
   P=-1324: printing and text extraction are permitted, while modification,
   annotation and document assembly (splitting/recombining pages) are denied.
   Redistributing rebuilt or extracted PDF pages would violate those permissions
   and the copyright in the drawings.

4. What IS included
   Structured, derived data: designator indexes, part-number/description fields,
   board coordinates, signal-chain ordering, fault-tree reasoning, page-number
   references, and SHORT single-line quotations attached to individual records
   solely so that a numeric value or designator can be verified against the
   source manual. Coverage labels identify the provenance of every record:
     manual         - verbatim short quote from the PDF text layer
     derived        - engineering inference built on manual evidence
     not_in_manual  - requested data absent from the manual

5. Accuracy and limitations
   The manual contains no troubleshooting section, no component-level DC
   voltage table, no waveforms and no tolerance specifications. Values that
   are absent are represented as null and labelled "not_in_manual"; they must
   not be filled with assumed figures. Power-net labels such as 14V, 8V, 5V,
   3R3V are NET NAMES; any nominal voltage derived from a name is explicitly
   flagged as inferred and is not a measured value or a tolerance.

